; Fixed runtime workspace outside the 14,200-byte interpreter image.  The
; cold-start initializer assigns the dynamic arena and dictionary partition;
; the remaining cells below have stable roles across parser, supervisor and
; device subsystems.
; Workspace orientation
; ---------------------
; The fixed workspace is the interpreter's set of global roots and scratch
; cells.  The dynamic region above it is a two-ended arena:
;
;       low addresses                                  high addresses
;       +------------------ free gap -------------------------------+
;       ^ execution frames grow upward       heap objects grow downward ^
;       EXECUTION_TOP                                 TERM_HEAP_CURSOR
;
; A name-pool partition sits below that arena and is managed by a bitmap.  Words
; named *_ROOT keep objects alive; words named *_CURSOR or *_TOP are allocation
; boundaries; callback targets are self-patched JP operands.  See
; analysis/MEMORY_MAP.md for the complete address map and module 12 for the cold
; start code that initializes these cells.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; WORKSPACE OWNERSHIP MAP
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; Nearby addresses are not necessarily one data structure.  The fixed workspace
; is better read as four ownership bands:
;
;   protected native state
;       SUPERVISOR_MACHINE_STACK, ROM error return, saved callbacks
;
;   hot logical-machine state
;       EXEC_* words, current frame, choice point, trail and arena frontiers
;
;   parser / printer / primitive scratch
;       token buffer, variable maps, decimal workspaces, argument slots
;
;   device and persistent workspace state
;       current module dictionaries, file-control block, line-editor buffer
;
; Each later chapter names the subset it owns.  Physical adjacency here is a
; consequence of fitting the machine into RAM, not evidence of semantic unity.
SUPERVISOR_MACHINE_STACK:          equ 09803h
EXEC_ARENA_LIMIT:                  equ 09837h
PRIMITIVE_DISPATCH_SLOT_CURSOR:    equ 09861h
CONSOLE_COPY_TO_PRINTER:           equ 0996fh
LINE_EDITOR_CURSOR_LETTER:         equ 09970h
LINE_EDITOR_READ_INDEX:            equ 09971h
LINE_EDITOR_LENGTH:                equ 09972h
LINE_EDITOR_BUFFER:                equ 09973h
LINE_EDITOR_BUFFER_CAPACITY:       equ 0fah
TYPEAHEAD_COUNT:                   equ 09a73h
TYPEAHEAD_BUFFER:                  equ 09a74h
TYPEAHEAD_CAPACITY:                equ 010h
RDR_PUSHBACK_BYTE:                 equ 09a84h
DISPLAY_LAST_TEXT_ROW:             equ 09b6ch
DICTIONARY_NAME_POOL_START:        equ 09da5h

